---
import { EMAIL } from '../lib/site';
---

<section class="about" id="about">
  <div class="about-label">About</div>

  <div class="about-body">
    <p>
      I'm Ryodgie ( ree-yoh-jee ). It rhymes with nothing. 
    </p>
    <p>
      Front-end designer and developer. I chase editorial layouts, typefaces, and grids that actually hold, then go build the thing in Astro, React, or Vue. Sometimes I wander into the backend to see where the data's coming from, or poke at AI tools and lose an afternoon.
    </p>
    <p>
      I can't look at a menu, a poster or a badly kerned shopfront without rebuilding it in my head. This has been happening since long before anyone paid me for it. Most of the work on this page comes from exactly that — no client, no brief, no one telling me the logo should be bigger. Just things I wanted to see exist.
    </p>
    <p>
      I got here sideways. I spent a decade in customer experience for major
      publications like <span class="highlight">Tribune Publishing</span> and the <span class="highlight">Los Angeles Times</span>. Eventually, I made the
      pivot—doing front-end at <span class="highlight">MC2</span>, then visual design for AI training models at <span class="highlight">Wirestock</span>.
      Different rooms, same instinct — noticing when something's off and wanting to fix it.
    </p>
    <p class="about-cta">
        I make things nobody asked for. Ask me for something — <a class="email" href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>